title: 'statement network: score peers by behaviour to steer disconnects'

doc:
- audience: Node Operator
  description: |-
    With the v2 DHT path enabled (`STATEMENT_STORE_V2_DHT_ENABLED=1`), peer steering
    disconnects the worst-behaved statement peers first instead of the longest-connected.
    Each connected peer carries a score that rises on a valid statement and drops twice as
    much on an invalid, duplicate, or undecodable one; outcomes caused by the local node
    leave it unchanged. The score resets when the peer's substream closes. Without the flag,
    behavior is unchanged.

crates:
- name: sc-network-statement
  bump: minor
